      "when": "c. 300 BC–AD 300",
      "text": "Rome's great roads fanned out from the city. The Via Appia ran south to Capua and on to Brundisium, the Flaminia crossed the Apennines to the Adriatic, the Aurelia followed the coast to the north-west. Itiner-e, a new digital atlas of Roman roads, maps almost 600 km of the Via Appia alone.",
